<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n73236" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλολῡγ-μός</span></b> , ὁ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>loud cry,</i> mostly
				<i>of joy,</i> in honour of the gods, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. ἱρὸν . . παιώνισον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					268
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀ. εὐφημοῦντα τῇδε λαμπάδι
					ἐπορθιάζειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				595
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Or.</u>
				1137
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ze.</u>
				1.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Lond.</u>
				121.323
			</span></i> : pl., <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				143
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				419
			</span></i> ; <i>song of triumph,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφυμνῆσαι . . ὀ. ἀνδρὸς θεινομένου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					387
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.) ; rarely of <i>lamentation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				7.182
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Mel.
			</span></i>).</div>
